    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nTake the following `custom_textobjects` config:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\ncustom_textobjects = {\r\n            xv = spec_treesitter { a = \"@pair.value\", i = \"@pair.value\" },\r\n        }\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhere the `@pair.value` looks like the following for Lua:\r\n\r\n```scheme\r\n(table_constructor\r\n  (field\r\n    value: [(string) (attribute) (identifier) (function_call) (function_definition)] @pair.value))\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the key (xv) is only a single character (tested with `x` and `v`), the capture is recognised and managed by mini.ai, otherwise not.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-2488+g5d4e1693c Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1707061634\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nAttached tarball has the necessary files. Open with the following command:\r\n\r\nNVIM_DATA_MINIMAL=/tmp/minimal NVIM_APP_NAME=\"nvim-minimal\" nvim -u minimal.lua\r\n\r\nExit, then open `test.lua`\r\n\r\nIt contains the following:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal t = {\r\n    key = \"value\",\r\n    otherkey = {\r\n        [\"nested_table_key\"] = \"someotherstuff\",\r\n    },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nMove your cursor onto \"nested_table_key\"\r\nType `viNxv`\r\nIt should select the \"value\" up above\r\n\r\nOpen minimal.lua and replace the 'xv' key in mini.ai setup with 'x'\r\n\r\nWhen tried again, it selects \"value\" as expected.\r\n\r\n[minimal.tar.gz](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/files/14653530/minimal.tar.gz)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nTwo character capture triggers are recognised\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nTwo character capture triggers are not recognised",
