        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Would it be possible to convert the issue into a feature request then? I'd be happy to hack something together!\r\n\r\nSorry, no. There is no good way to implement this feature under current design.\r\n\r\nThe main issue here is that it should be allowed to spend any amount of time to enter textobject identifier. If that is the case, then if more than one character for textobject identifier is allowed, then there should be a mechanism to know when a single character (majority of cases) is the target. Which itself implies that there should be at least an extra keystroke to tell 'mini.ai' that current input is the final textobject id, and that is bad.",
